.Dd October 6, 2026
.Dt BHOTKEYS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bhotkeys
.Nd plugin hotkey listener
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl Fl daemon
.Op Fl Fl greeter
.Op Fl Fl wm Ar name
.Nm
.Fl Fl panel
.Op Fl Fl greeter
.Nm
.Fl Fl print-keys Ar format
.Op Fl Fl wm Ar name
.Nm
.Fl Fl print-wm
.Op Fl Fl wm Ar name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
watches key presses through the X Record extension and runs the
command of the plugin whose chord matches.
It does not grab the keyboard in normal operation, and it does not
consume the event, so the window manager and every other client
still see the key.
Each window manager has an apply script in
.Pa @PREFIX@/libexec/bhotkeys .
It reads
.Fl Fl print-keys
and registers each chord the listener handles with the window
manager, to run
.Pa /usr/bin/true .
The window manager grabs that chord, so the focused client does not
see it.
A chord the window manager already owns is left alone.
The keyboard is grabbed only while the chord list is capturing a
new chord.
.Pp
No action ships with
.Nm
except the chords that open the list.
.Sy Panel
defaults to
.Sy Super+? .
It has no check box.
The chord can be changed.
It stays on until
.Nm bhotkeys-panel
.Fl Fl disable .
.Sy Panel alt
is
.Sy Super+/
by default.
Its check box turns that chord off.
Every other chord comes from a plugin.
If a list chord has been changed or forgotten,
.Nm
.Fl Fl panel
opens the list anyway.
.Pp
One listener serves one X display.
The greeter runs a separate listener
.Pq Fl Fl greeter
and does not share a process with the session.
A second session listener finds the lock held and exits.
The listener re-reads plugins when the session file's modification
time changes.
Opening the list always reads the plugins anew.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "--print-keys"
.It Fl Fl daemon
Listen on
.Ev DISPLAY .
If no known window manager is running yet, wait up to 30 seconds for
one before loading plugins, so that
.Li enabled ,
.Li chord ,
and
.Li session
lines resolve as the chord list will later see them.
.Fl Fl wm
skips the wait.
With
.Fl Fl greeter ,
listen for the login greeter.
.It Fl Fl greeter
Select the greeter.
Plugins marked
.Li greeter 0
are ignored.
Overrides are read from
.Pa @PREFIX@/etc/bhotkeys/greeter .
The list opened for the greeter is read-only until its unlock
password is entered.
See
.Xr bhotkeys-passwd 1 .
.Xr bhotkeys-greeter 1
starts and stops this listener.
.It Fl Fl panel
Open the chord list on the monitor under the pointer.
The list process is
.Nm bhotkeys-panel .
With
.Fl Fl greeter ,
the list is the greeter's read-only list.
.It Fl Fl print-keys Ar format
Print the chords spelled for one window manager, then exit.
.Ar format
is one of
.Cm bvwm , cinnamon , dwm , fluxbox , fvwm , gnome , i3 , kde ,
.Cm lxde , lxqt , mate , openbox , windowmaker , xfce ,
or
.Cm xmonad .
.Pp
Every format except
.Cm fvwm
and
.Cm bvwm
prints one tab-separated row per plugin shown in this session:
the
.Li id ,
the
.Li listen
field, the enabled state
.Pq Li 0 No or Li 1 ,
the chord as that window manager's configuration writes it, and the
label.
.Cm kde
adds the Qt key code before the label.
A
.Li listen 1
chord on an XF86 key is left out: it inserts no character, so there
is nothing to swallow.
Panel and Panel alt are
.Li listen 1
rows.
No column is empty.
.Pp
.Cm fvwm
and
.Cm bvwm
print
.Xr fvwm 1
.Cm Key
lines for every plugin shown in this session, and for Panel and
Panel alt.
A plugin whose
.Li listen
field is 0 is a window manager key: its action is the plugin
command, run through
.Nm bhotkeys-bvwm-run .
A plugin whose
.Li listen
field is 1 is a listener key: its action is
.Cm Nop ,
so the window manager grabs the chord and the focused client does
not see it.
XF86 keys are included.
A disabled plugin of either kind is printed with the action
.Ql - ,
which unbinds the chord; those lines print first.
A
.Li listen 0
plugin with no command only documents a key the window manager
owns, and is not printed.
.It Fl Fl print-wm
Print the name of the running window manager, then exit.
If none is running yet, wait up to 30 seconds.
The name is the one
.Fl Fl daemon
uses for
.Li enabled ,
.Li chord ,
and
.Li session
lines.
When none appears in that time, exit 1.
.Fl Fl wm
prints that name without waiting.
.It Fl Fl wm Ar name
Treat
.Ar name
as the running window manager instead of detecting one.
.Ar name
is one of the window manager names a plugin may use on its
.Li chord ,
.Li enabled ,
and
.Li session
lines, matched without regard to case.
Program-name tokens on those lines still match the running commands.
This masters one window manager's files from another, as when the
first cannot start.
An unknown
.Ar name
is an error.
.El
.Pp
An unrecognized option, or no options, prints the usage and exits non-zero.
.Sh PANEL
The list is an overlay.
.Sy Esc
closes it.
A check enables or disables that plugin.
.Sy "Set keys"
grabs the keyboard until the next chord, which is stored for that
row.
.Sy Reset
puts back the chord selected for the running window manager.
The check box is left as it was saved.
.Sy Window
hands the same list to the window manager as an ordinary decorated
window, and
.Sy Overlay
turns it back.
A plugin whose
.Li id
is
.Li lock
closes the overlay before its command runs, and leaves a decorated
list window alone.
.Pp
Column headings sort the rows.
The same heading cycles through ascending, descending, and no sort.
With no sort, rows are ordered by the group string, then by name.
The built-in list has two rows and no plugin file.
Their heading is
.Li x11/bhotkeys .
Panel has no check box.
The Panel alt check box turns its chord off.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Nm bhotkeys-panel Fl Fl disable
Turns the Panel and Panel alt chords off, so no chord opens the
list.
The running listener picks up the change.
.Nm
.Fl Fl panel
still opens the list, and does not turn either chord back on.
.It Nm bhotkeys-panel Fl Fl enable
Turns both chords back on.
.El
.Pp
Add
.Fl Fl greeter
to either command to change the greeter instead of the session.
That write requires the super-user.
An open list is closed by
.Fl Fl disable ,
including one that was handed to the window manager.
.Sh PLUGINS
A plugin is a text file.
One file describes one plugin.
Blank lines and lines beginning with
.Ql #
are ignored.
The listener scans
.Pa @PREFIX@/share/bhotkeys/plugins.d ,
then
.Pa ~/share/bhotkeys/plugins.d ,
then the directory named by
.Ev BHOTKEYS_PLUGINS .
A later directory replaces the same
.Li id .
The user's directory overrides a system plugin, and
.Ev BHOTKEYS_PLUGINS
overrides both.
.Pp
A field is a keyword, a space, and the rest of the line:
.Bl -tag -width "command"
.It Li id
Required name.
A plugin with
.Li listen 1
also requires
.Li command .
.It Li label
Text shown in the list.
Defaults to
.Li id .
.It Li group
The list heading, shown exactly as written.
Nothing is prefixed or renamed.
An omitted group is a blank heading.
.It Li chord
Chord for this plugin.
More than one
.Li chord
line is allowed.
See
.Sx "Chords and window managers"
below.
.It Li enabled
.Li 0
or
.Li 1 .
More than one line is allowed, with the same window-manager rule
as
.Li chord .
No
.Li enabled
line means on.
.It Li command
Command run when the chord matches.
The rest of the line is the command.
.It Li repeat
Non-zero repeats the command while the chord is held.
A command still running does not start another copy; further
repeats wait, and releasing the chord stops them.
The default is 0.
.It Li greeter
.Li 1
if the greeter listener may run this plugin.
The default is 0.
.It Li session
.Li 0
hides the plugin from a user session.
.Li 1
shows it.
More than one line is allowed, with the same window-manager rule
as
.Li chord .
No
.Li session
line means shown.
The greeter list uses
.Li greeter
instead.
.It Li listen
.Li 0
shows the plugin in the list and in
.Fl Fl print-keys ,
and
.Nm
does not listen for it.
The default is 1.
.It Li desc
One line of description, searched from the list.
.It Li desc_greeter
Optional description shown when the list is the greeter.
When the line is absent, the greeter shows
.Li desc .
.El
.Ss Chords and window managers
A chord is zero or more of
.Sy Super+ ,
.Sy Alt+ ,
.Sy Shift+ ,
and
.Sy Ctrl+ ,
then a keysym name.
Spaces are ignored.
The names
.Li slash ,
.Li space ,
.Li question ,
and
.Li grave
are slash, Space, question mark, and grave accent.
A single letter is that letter.
Anything else is passed to
.Fn XStringToKeysym .
.Pp
Tokens after the chord name the window managers that line is for.
The word
.Li default
is a fallback, not a manager name.
A line with no tokens after the chord is also a fallback; the word
is needed only to make a line that names managers a fallback as
well.
The first line that names the running manager is used, even when a
fallback line is written above it.
If none names it, the first fallback is used.
Two fallbacks: the first one wins.
A line that only names other managers is not a fallback, so the
plugin can have no chord on this manager.
A chord that does not parse disables the plugin.
.Pp
The known names, matched case-insensitively, are
.Cm afterstep ,
.Cm awesome ,
.Cm bspwm ,
.Cm bvwm ,
.Cm cinnamon ,
.Cm cwm ,
.Cm dwm ,
.Cm enlightenment ,
.Cm fluxbox ,
.Cm fvwm ,
.Cm gnome ,
.Cm herbstluftwm ,
.Cm i3 ,
.Cm icewm ,
.Cm jwm ,
.Cm kde ,
.Cm lxde ,
.Cm lxqt ,
.Cm mate ,
.Cm openbox ,
.Cm pekwm ,
.Cm spectrwm ,
.Cm sway ,
.Cm windowmaker ,
and
.Cm xfce .
.Cm bvwm
is not
.Cm fvwm .
If both are running,
.Cm bvwm
wins.
.Cm fvwm
matches
.Sy fvwm ,
.Sy fvwm2 ,
or
.Sy fvwm3 .
.Cm kde
matches KWin, not a process named
.Ql kde .
.Cm gnome
matches
.Sy gnome-shell .
.Cm xfce
matches
.Sy xfwm4 .
.Cm windowmaker
matches
.Sy wmaker .
.Cm cinnamon
matches
.Sy cinnamon
or
.Sy muffin .
.Cm mate
matches
.Sy marco .
.Cm lxde
matches
.Sy lxsession .
.Cm lxqt
matches
.Sy lxqt-session .
Those two are checked before
.Cm kde ,
.Cm gnome ,
.Cm xfce ,
and
.Cm openbox ,
so a session that runs one of those as its window manager is still
.Cm lxde
or
.Cm lxqt .
A token that is not one of these names is a command name, matched
case-sensitively against a running command.
.Pp
.Li enabled
and
.Li session
use the same rule.
The first token of either is
.Li 0
or
.Li 1 ,
and only those two values are accepted.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
chord Super+e
chord Super+Shift+e kde
enabled 1
enabled 0 gnome
session 1
session 0 xfce
.Ed
.Pp
On KDE the chord is
.Sy Super+Shift+e ;
everywhere else it is
.Sy Super+e .
On GNOME the plugin is off; elsewhere it is on.
The row is hidden on Xfce, where neither the chord nor the enabled
bit matters, and shown on every other manager.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
chord Super+e default fvwm
chord Super+Shift+e kde
.Ed
.Pp
makes
.Sy Super+e
the fvwm chord and the fallback for every other manager, and
.Sy Super+Shift+e
the KDE chord.
Without the word, the first line would be fvwm only and a third line
would be needed for the fallback.
.Pp
Once the plugin file has picked a chord and an enabled bit for the
running window manager, a session file line that names that manager
replaces both.
A line saved under one manager does not apply under another.
It leaves
.Li session
as written in the plugin file.
Each line is
.Pp
.Dl id enabled chord wm
.Pp
and the list's own lines are
.Pp
.Dl panel enabled chord wm
.Dl panel-alt enabled chord wm
.Pp
.Li panel
.Li enabled
is 0 when the Panel chord does not open the list.
.Li panel-alt
.Li enabled
is 0 when the Panel alt chord does not open the list.
With no such line for this manager, that chord is on.
A line with no window manager name is ignored.
.Sy Reset
restores the window-manager chord.
It does not change the check box.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "BHOTKEYS_PLUGINS"
.It Ev DISPLAY
X server to watch.
.It Ev BHOTKEYS_GREETER
Set to
.Li 1
for a command run by the greeter listener.
.It Ev BHOTKEYS_PLUGINS
Extra plugin directory, scanned last.
A file here replaces the same
.Li id
from either directory above.
.It Ev HOME
Used for
.Pa ~/share/bhotkeys/plugins.d ,
.Pa ~/.config/bhotkeys/session ,
and
.Pa ~/.config/bhotkeys/panel-ui
when
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
When set, the session file is
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bhotkeys/session .
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory of the session lock,
.Pa bhotkeys.lock .
When unset, the lock is
.Pa /tmp/bhotkeys.lock .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "@PREFIX@/share/bhotkeys/plugins.d"
.It Pa @PREFIX@/share/bhotkeys/plugins.d
First plugin directory.
.It Pa ~/share/bhotkeys/plugins.d
Second plugin directory.
.It Pa ~/.config/bhotkeys/session
Session overrides.
See
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
.It Pa ~/.config/bhotkeys/panel-ui
List sort and scroll.
Not read at the greeter.
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/bhotkeys/greeter
Greeter overrides. Lines have no window manager name.
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/bhotkeys.passwd
Greeter unlock hash.
See
.Xr bhotkeys-passwd 1 .
.It Pa /tmp/bhotkeys-greeter.lock
Greeter listener lock.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
The session listener exits 0 when another session listener already
holds the lock.
It exits non-zero when it cannot open the display or the Record
extension is missing.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys-greeter 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys-panel 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys-passwd 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys-start 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
